# a program's word of a module word's name and arity answers the program's calls; another word of the module keeps
# the module's own (decision library-words-lexical), so math's distance still calls math's norm
'use math; norm(x) := 99; distance([3, 4], [0, 0])'	5
'use math; clamp(x) := 9; clamp(5)'	9
'use math; lerp(a, b, t) := 0; lerp(1, 2, 0.5)'	0
